    "turn_text": "Yeah, I don't buy it at all either. And I mean, you go back to the Blue Ribbon Commission and even back in the days of Carter, or not in the days of Carter, but in early 2000, the commission that he did, one of the issues that they came up with was that mail-in ballots, which is part of their early voting, opened the doors for fraud. I mean, that was coming from Democrats at that point. And now all of a sudden, no, no, no, no, they push for more and more and more of this thing. But it's voter identification, it's the lack of clean voter rolls. It's the, you know, just one thing after another, the ballot harvesting, all these things",
